// A name in the braces of a class pattern is a field name, and the arm binds
// it to the value of that field (spec/04-semantics.md, match Expression,
// "Constructor patterns": a bare name in braces is a binding). This is so
// also when an enum constructor has the same name: the tag test applies
// only to the name before the braces, not to the field names.
enum Color { Red }
class Box {
    init(v) { this.Red = v; }
}

print match Box(42) {
    case Box{Red} => "field " + str(Red)
    case _ => "no match"
};

// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: field 42
